    1179,
    2556
   ],
   "product_base_commit": "4afc6d2a9ef4eae9e94c5b3a4f74ced5aa5ae2da",
   "capture": "iPhone 16 simulator, iOS 26.5. simctl captured the screen during a downward XCUITest drag on the hourly header in PlacesUITests.testDraggingAChartScrollsOnlyTheChart, fixture mode. The test confirmed one additional local weather request and the same place (Busan) after release."
  }
 ],
 "source_changes": [
  {
   "date": "2026-11-18",
   "source": "ios/tools/manual/run-manual-capture.sh",
   "change": "after manual-11 the export step fails the run on a failed export, a missing attachment manifest or a screenshot set other than the test's own 41 shot names in ManualUITests.swift (review findings CODEX-IN18P3-1 and -4); the test, the simulator set-up and the image reduction are unchanged, so the published screenshots stand"
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "source": "ios/tools/manual/run-manual-capture.sh, ios/TodayWeatherUITests/ManualUITests.swift",
   "change": "#3122: --no-ads builds without ad units and the test checks every screenshot (except over the system share sheet) for native ads; --store adds testCaptureTheStoreScreens for the App Store images. All 41 journey screenshots were recaptured with --no-ads; the share sheet did not appear on the capture simulators, so the last page shows the share button."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "source": "ios/tools/manual/run-manual-capture.sh",
   "change": "after the capture (review findings CODEX-3124-5, rounds 1 and 2) the ad-unit guard parses Info.plist, requires each key and Google's test app ID (the Debug value) in both modes, both units empty for --no-ads and the test units otherwise; the build settings, test and image reduction are unchanged, so the screenshots stand (the iPhone store run was repeated with the round-1 guard)"
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "source": "ios/TodayWeatherUITests/ManualUITests.swift",
   "change": "after the capture (#3122 widget images) testCaptureTheStoreScreens adds a Home Screen widget step (removeOtherWidgets, addWidget) and shot() skips the ad check on the Home Screen; testCaptureTheManual is unchanged, so the manual screenshots stand"
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "source": "ios/tools/manual/run-manual-capture.sh",
   "change": "after the capture (review finding CODEX-3124-15) --store runs on a disposable clone of the given simulator; the manual mode is unchanged, so the manual screenshots stand"
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "source": "ios/tools/manual/run-manual-capture.sh",
   "change": "after the capture (review round 7) --store creates its own simulator from the given one's device type and runtime and deletes it on exit, replacing the clone; the manual mode is unchanged, so the manual screenshots stand"
  }
 ]
}
